PROBLEM STATEMENT:
Given an integer array nums, calculate the running sum of the array.
The running sum at index i is calculated as:
runningSum[i] = nums[0] + nums[1] + ... + nums[i]
Return the resulting array.
AIM:To calculate the running sum of an array using a loop in Java.
JAVA CODE:
class Solution {
    public int[] runningSum(int[] nums) {

        int sum = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            sum = sum + nums[i];
            nums[i] = sum;
        }

        return nums;
    }
}
INPUT:
nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]
OUTPUT:
[1, 3, 6, 10]
